# Softmax of a vector, as X_eTaL-ML's NN library writes it: subtract the
# max (one reduction), exponentiate, divide by the sum (a second reduction).
# Three fused kernel stages separated by the two reductions. The sum of the
# probabilities is a third reduction, as a check.
%x = input f32 [1024]
%m = reduce max %x
%c = map sub %x %m
%e = map exp %c
%s = reduce add %e
%p = map div %e %s
%total = reduce add %p
output %p
output %total
